WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.020
Authentication review asks how the application establishes identity and whether that identity is verified consistently.

2
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:19.160
In a Node.js API, identity may come from a session cookie, bearer token, JWT, API key, service credential, or upstream identity provider.

3
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:29.100
AI can help locate where tokens are parsed, where signatures and expiration are checked, where request.user is populated, and which routes rely on that value.

4
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.720
The reviewer must verify that the code actually enforces those checks in the request path being changed.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.440
Authorization review asks a different question: is the verified identity allowed to perform this action on this specific object.

6
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.220
Authentication is not a substitute for authorization.

7
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.000
A user requesting a document by ID may be logged in and still have no right to read that document.

8
00:00:52.100 --> 00:01:05.620
AI can help trace object identifiers from req.params, req.query, or req.body into database calls and point out where the code checks ownership, tenant, role, or permission.

9
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:13.000
The reviewer should look for role checks without object checks and tenant filters that are applied in one path but missing in another.

10
00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.880
Session behavior deserves careful review because small inconsistencies can undermine access control.

11
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:31.220
Review cookie flags, session invalidation, password reset behavior, token refresh, logout, API key handling, service-to-service credentials, and administrative assumptions.

12
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:40.680
If AI suggests that a route appears protected, ask it to identify the exact middleware or guard, the files involved, and the data flow that proves enforcement.

13
00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:48.220
A useful finding explains where the identity is created, where permission is checked, and where the sensitive action happens.
